#title[Dirichlet series of dirichlet product of species is dirchlet product of dirichlet series]

$
  D_(F *_D G) (S) (n) = (D_F (S) *_D D_G (S))(n)
$

i.e
$
  (|(F *_D G)([n])|)/(n!) n^(-|S|) =
  plus.big_(sum (k,l : NN), k*l=n) (|F([k])|)/(k!) k^(-|S|) *
  (|G([l])|)/(l!) l^(-|S|) 
$

clearly
$
  plus.big_(sum (k,l : NN), k*l=n) (|F([k])|)/(k!) k^(-|S|) *
  (|G([l])|)/(l!) l^(-|S|) =

  plus.big_(sum (k,l : NN), k*l=n) (|F([k])|)/(k!) *
  (|G([l])|)/(l!) n^(-|S|)
$

To continue here we must first make progress on the groupoid cardinality of the dirichlet product of F and G, for that look at group action of $S_n$ on cartesian decompositions
